    "updated_at": "2021-10-20T20:43:52Z",
    "body": "@achristensen07 `new URL('https://a\\u0007f.com')` is `a` U+0007 `f`, while `'a' + String.fromCodePoint(0x7F)` is `a` U+007F.\r\n\r\nI guess I was wrong in my initial post (which I've just updated): Firefox forbids `%00`–`%1F`, `%7F`, and `\\u0000`–`\\u001F`. It does not forbid `\\u007F`. Chrome forbids all of these.\r\n\r\nI propose that we follow Chrome here as it's more consistent.\r\n\r\nEdit: Oops, GitHub didn't update to show @valenting's comment before I posted :)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
