    "updated_at": "2021-11-14T12:18:26Z",
    "body": "The standard currently allows any string to be used as an opaque-host, if appropriately percent-encoded. \r\nIsn't it a bit strange to add a special case for only the percent-encoded-bytes that decode to C0 and DEL codepoints?\r\n\r\nI had a look at making the change, but it turns out to be more complex than anticipated, of course :/",
