      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2021-11-15T08:17:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-15T08:17:49Z",
    "body": "If I understood the proposal correctly, percent-encoded control code points in the hosts would cause the parser to fail. \r\n\r\nIf that is extended to opaque hosts as well, that would mean that e.g. `sc://a%01` would fail, even though, e.g. `sc://a%35` does not. (`%35` decodes to `#`).\r\n\r\nI think it is better to allow any percent-encoded bytes in opaque hosts. \r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
