    "created_at": "2021-11-15T10:54:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-15T10:54:45Z",
    "body": "It should be a concern, because it would make them even less backwards compatible. Which makes it less likely they can adopt the better approach.\r\n\r\nI don't think we should change the opaque-host parser from what it does now. This change is not about that.\r\n\r\nAs for the setter, that also seems like a separate discussion. Unless there's a compelling use case I don't really see the need personally.",
